<$fill $name="body">

!! Keys

|!Shortcut tiddler |!Default |!Action |
|`outline-up` / `outline-down` |Up / Down |Select previous / next unit. A whole list counts as one block: Down from a selected list goes to the block after it, Up from below a list selects the whole list; inside a list they go item by item |
|`outline-up-deep` / `outline-down-deep` |ctrl-Up / ctrl-Down |Select previous / next unit in document order, also into lists (from below a list: its last item) |
|`outline-parent` / `outline-child` |Left / Right |Select the parent unit (item of a sub-item, whole list of a top-level item, heading of a section) / the first child |
|`outline-move-up` / `outline-move-down` |alt-Up / alt-Down |Swap with previous / next sibling |
|`outline-indent` / `outline-promote` |Tab / shift-Tab |Demote / promote by one level |
|`outline-edit` |Enter |Edit in place (on a transclusion Enter opens the target) |
|`outline-menu` |shift-Enter |Block menu: insert a new block after the unit, or turn it into another type; Up/Down, Enter runs, Escape closes |
|`outline-open` |Enter |Open the transclusion target in outline mode |
|`outline-clear` |Escape |Clear selection |
|`outline-save` |ctrl-Enter |Save the edit |
|`outline-continue` |Enter |Save and open a new unit (single-line units) |
|`outline-newline` |shift-Enter |Newline in the editor (saved as `<br>` in list items and headings) |
|`outline-indent` / `outline-promote` |Tab / shift-Tab |In the editor too: save, indent / promote, keep editing |
|`outline-move-up` / `outline-move-down` |alt-Up / alt-Down |In the editor too: save, move, keep editing |
|`outline-edit-up` |ctrl-Up |Editor only: save and edit the previous unit |
|`outline-edit-down` |ctrl-Down |Editor only: save and edit the next unit |
|`outline-cancel` |Escape |Discard the edit |
|`outline-help` |shift-slash |Show / hide the key overview. `?` always works too, whatever the keyboard layout; Escape closes it |

All are `$:/config/shortcuts/<name>`; descriptions are in `$:/config/ShortcutInfo/<name>`. Change them in the settings tab (the core shortcut editor, press the key to record it, platform variants included) or in ControlPanel > Keyboard Shortcuts.

!! Type badges

|!`data-ol-type` |!Unit |
|`paragraph`, `code-block`, `table`, `quote`, `rule` |Blocks (`p`, `pre`, `table`, `blockquote`, `hr`; other blocks: their tag name) |
|`h1` … `h6` |Headings |
|`bullet`, `numbered`, `term`, `definition`, `quote` |List items (by their list: `ul`, `ol`, `dt`/`dd`, `blockquote`) |
|`bullet-list`, `numbered-list`, `definitions`, `quote` |Whole lists (badge in the left margin) |
|`transclusion`, `widget` |Transclusion lines, widgets and macro calls |
|tag name (`div`, ...) |Opened HTML containers (badge in the left margin) |

The widget sets `data-ol-type` on each unit's first DOM node (`unitType` in `dom-utils.js`); CSS shows it as `::after`, absolutely positioned, so the layout does not change. The editor field gets the type of the unit it edits, of the chosen block type, or of its anchor (a new item); an item edited inside its `li` keeps the `li`'s badge.

!! Key overview

The //keys// tab and the overlay (`?` in an outline, or the small ? button at its top right) show the same table, `$:/plugins/rimir/outline/ui/keys-table`, with the keys read live from the config. Its groups are the tiddlers listed in `$:/plugins/rimir/outline/key-groups`: each has a `caption`, an optional `hint`, a `list` of shortcut names and, optionally, text shown after the keys (the fixed block menu keys). The settings tab uses the same groups.

In multi-line units (code blocks, tables, widgets, `"""` items) Enter is a plain newline and only Ctrl-Enter saves.

!! Indent and promote

* Lists: a list item and its subtree lines get one more of the item's last marker character (`#b` becomes `##b`, `*b` `**b`, `#*` `#**`). No previous sibling: no-op. Promote removes one marker character; depth 1 is a no-op.
* Headings: one `!` more on the heading and every heading in its section; no-op if one would pass 6. Promote removes one; level 1 is a no-op.
* Other units: Tab and Shift-Tab do nothing.

!! Move

Swap the unit's whole subtree with the adjacent sibling's whole subtree, blank-line separators preserved. Blocks other than items and headings that touch (a single line break) get a blank line between them and before the following content, so a paragraph cannot absorb its neighbour. First/last child: no-op.

* List item: siblings are items of the same list at the same depth.
* Heading: siblings are headings of the same level in the same parent.
* Other blocks: siblings are blocks in the same section (or HTML container, or root) before any sub-heading.

!! New unit (Enter)

* List item: same marker, after the item's whole subtree.
* Heading: paragraph directly under the heading line.
* Paragraph: paragraph after it.

!! Block menu

|!Selected |!Insert after |!Turn into |
|Paragraph |Paragraph, Heading 1–3, Bulleted/Numbered list, Quote, Code block |Heading 1–3, Bulleted/Numbered list, Quote, Code block |
|Heading |the same (a heading goes after the section, other blocks right below the heading) |Paragraph, Bulleted/Numbered list, Quote, Code block |
|Code block |the same |Paragraph, Bulleted/Numbered list, Quote |
|Whole list |the same |Bulleted ↔ Numbered (all levels) |
|List item |– |Bulleted ↔ Numbered (with all its siblings of that level) |
|Transclusion |the same, plus //Edit this line// first |– |

!! State and config

|!Tiddler |!Purpose |
|`$:/state/rimir/outline/on/<title>` |Outline mode on (`yes`) / off |
|`$:/temp/rimir/outline/...` |Editor buffer, selection and open key overview (`help/<title>`) while active |
|`$:/config/rimir/outline/badges` |Type badges: `all` (default), `headings` (h1–h6 only) or `off`. Sets class `rr-ol-badges-<mode>` on the frame; the badge text is the unit's `data-ol-type` |
|`$:/config/rimir/outline/full-editor` |`yes`: full text editor with toolbar; otherwise (default `no`) the compact one-line editor |

